@@ -34,6 +34,11 @@ You can find our backwards-compatibility policy [here](https://github.com/hynek/
 
   [#657](https://github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/657)
 
+- `structlog.processors.ExceptionRenderer` (and therefore `structlog.processors.format_exc_info` and `structlog.processors.dict_tracebacks`) doesn't add an `exception` key anymore if there's no exception to render -- for example, if `logger.exception()` is called outside of an exception handler.
+  Previously, the `exception` key was set to `"MISSING"` or `[]`, respectively.
+
+  [#634](https://github.com/hynek/structlog/issues/634)
+
 - Instantiating `structlog.dev.ConsoleRenderer` does not mutate the passed *styles* dict anymore.
 
   [#669](https://github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/669)
